          <baseCommit>a03a041c3f8c1b739dfb1e51516de0b07da6e57b</baseCommit>
          <feedback>Stage 1 (&quot;Create Poem&quot;) completed as instructed. Execute rewrote blocks/org/blockml/bml/workspace/playground/NextPoem222.bml: the prior Spanish poem was replaced with a fresh, original German poem about a tree and a mushroom, the `&lt;is>` line updated to &quot;written in German&quot;, the documentation body replaced with the German verses, and the title property changed to &quot;Die Tanne und der Pilz&quot; (author unchanged: John Doe). Content matches the Stage 1 instruction (German poem about a tree and a mushroom, regenerated per execution) and the run parameters (language:&quot;German&quot;, author:&quot;John Doe&quot;). Only the playground block was modified; the ModelTransformation file under _meta/transform/running/ was read but not written. Structure/format of the block appears consistent with the previous version (same block name, type, baseType core:Documentation, properties layout).</feedback>
          <result>German-language poem &quot;Die Tanne und der Pilz&quot; (author: John Doe). At the forest edge stands an old, broad fir whose dark needled canopy holds summer light and time; its bark is grey and heavy with many years, yet it withstands storm, frost and driving rain. At its feet, still in the wet moss, grows a small bare mushroom with no defense, its brown cap barely glistening in the early dew, ducking from the wind in the grey expanse. The fir speaks to the little one: stay close, my shade cools when the midday glows hot, I spread my crown like a tent and shelter you when hard rain pours. So they grew through autumn and winter snow — the fir standing tall, the mushroom small in the clover — and whoever sits within their green spell finds two companions one can love.</result>
          <completedAt>2026-09-02T21:54:54</completedAt>
          <task>
            <workflow:InstructionTask instructions="Create or update the block org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.NextPoem222.bml that contains a random poem in german about a tree and a mushroom. For each execution create a new poem." />
          </task>
          <resultProducer>
            <running:T00013_PoemTestTemplate_20260902T215337.TestResultProducer />
          </resultProducer>
          <changedFiles>
            <type:FilePathEntity value="blocks/org/blockml/bml/workspace/playground/NextPoem222.bml" />
          </changedFiles>
        </workflow:Stage>
        <workflow:Stage name="Translate Poem" status="Succeeded">
          <startedAt>2026-09-02T21:54:55</startedAt>
          <baseCommit>c77f49d764b8c8f3cfcd487244355c51bd12dd7e</baseCommit>
          <feedback>Stage 2 (&quot;Translate Poem&quot;) completed as instructed. Execute rewrote blocks/org/blockml/bml/workspace/playground/NextPoem222.bml, translating the Stage 1 German poem &quot;Die Tanne und der Pilz&quot; into Spanish: the `&lt;is>` line was updated from &quot;written in German&quot; to &quot;written in Spanish&quot;; the four stanzas in the documentation body were replaced with faithful Spanish translations that preserve the tree-and-mushroom subject, the fir's speech to the mushroom, and the closing image of two companions; and the title property was changed to &quot;El abeto y el hongo&quot;. The author property is unchanged (John Doe). Block structure/format is consistent with the previous version (same name, type playground:NextPoem222, baseType core:Documentation, properties layout). Only the playground block was modified; no _meta/transform/ ModelTransformation files were touched by Execute (the running transformation file was read only). This matches the Stage 2 instruction (translate the poem to Spanish) and run parameters.</feedback>
          <completedAt>2026-09-02T21:55:48</completedAt>
          <task>
